<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Poster Infographic</title>
<style>
  body {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    background-color: #0b1120; /* Deep navy */
    color: #f8fafc;
    font-family: 'Inter', 'Helvetica Neue', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
    width: 2000px;
    height: 2828px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    box-sizing: border-box;
    padding: 80px 100px;
  }
  .header {
    text-align: center;
    margin-bottom: 60px;
  }
  .title {
    font-size: 80px;
    font-weight: 800;
    color: #38bdf8; /* electric blue */
    margin: 0 0 30px 0;
    line-height: 1.15;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 2px;
  }
  .citation {
    font-size: 36px;
    color: #94a3b8;
    background: rgba(56, 189, 248, 0.1);
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 15px 40px;
    border-radius: 40px;
    border: 2px solid #38bdf8;
  }
  .metrics-banner {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-around;
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, #1e293b 0%, #0f172a 100%);
    padding: 60px 40px;
    border-radius: 30px;
    margin-bottom: 60px;
    border-top: 8px solid #facc15; /* warm gold */
    box-shadow: 0 20px 40px rgba(0,0,0,0.5);
  }
  .metric {
    text-align: center;
    flex: 1;
    border-right: 2px solid #334155;
  }
  .metric:last-child {
    border-right: none;
  }
  .metric-value {
    font-size: 84px;
    font-weight: 900;
    color: #facc15; /* warm gold */
    margin-bottom: 15px;
    text-shadow: 0 4px 10px rgba(250, 204, 21, 0.3);
  }
  .metric-label {
    font-size: 30px;
    color: #e2e8f0;
    font-weight: 600;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 1px;
  }
  .content-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    grid-gap: 60px;
    flex: 1;
  }
  .section {
    background: rgba(30, 41, 59, 0.6);
    border-radius: 30px;
    padding: 50px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    border: 1px solid #334155;
  }
  .section.full-width {
    grid-column: 1 / -1;
  }
  .section.large-content {
    background: linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(30, 41, 59, 0.8) 0%, rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.8) 100%);
    border: 2px solid #2dd4bf;
  }
  .section-title {
    font-size: 48px;
    font-weight: 800;
    color: #2dd4bf; /* teal */
    margin-top: 0;
    margin-bottom: 40px;
    border-bottom: 4px solid #334155;
    padding-bottom: 20px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 2px;
  }
  .section-text {
    font-size: 32px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: #cbd5e1;
  }
  .section-text p {
    margin-top: 0;
    margin-bottom: 30px;
  }
  .section-text strong {
    color: #e2e8f0;
  }
  .ig-container {
    flex: 1;
    width: 100%;
    min-height: 500px;
  }
  .ig-container.large {
    min-height: 800px;
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>
  <div class="header">
    <h1 class="title">Mapping Neural Circuit Architecture:<br>Advances in Brain Connectivity Analysis</h1>
    <div class="citation">NATURE, 2024 | DOI: 10.1038/s41586-024-07487-w</div>
  </div>

  <div class="metrics-banner">
    <div class="metric">
      <div class="metric-value">~125,000</div>
      <div class="metric-label">Neurons Mapped</div>
    </div>
    <div class="metric">
      <div class="metric-value">~54M</div>
      <div class="metric-label">Synapses Catalogued</div>
    </div>
    <div class="metric">
      <div class="metric-value">37</div>
      <div class="metric-label">Circuit Motifs Identified</div>
    </div>
    <div class="metric">
      <div class="metric-value">94.2%</div>
      <div class="metric-label">Classification Accuracy</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="content-grid">
    <div class="section">
      <h2 class="section-title">Background & Motivation</h2>
      <div class="section-text">
        <p>Understanding how the brain processes information requires detailed maps of neural connectivity. While classical neuroanatomy provided foundational insights, the field lacked the resolution and scale needed to capture complete circuit-level wiring diagrams.</p>
        <p>Recent advances in <strong>electron microscopy</strong>, <strong>automated segmentation</strong>, and <strong>computational neuroscience</strong> have converged to make large-scale connectomics feasible. This landmark study bridges the gap between structural connectivity and functional organization.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
      <h2 class="section-title">Implications & Future Directions</h2>
      <div class="section-text">
        <p>These findings reshape our understanding of cortical computation. Modular connectivity motifs act as a finite vocabulary of circuit elements—analogous to logic gates.</p>
        <p>Hub neurons act as disproportionate drivers of network activity, directly impacting how we understand focal lesions, targeted stimulation, and BCI design.</p>
        <p>Future work will extend this connectomic approach to additional brain regions and species, with the ultimate goal of a complete mammalian wiring diagram.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section full-width">
      <h2 class="section-title" style="color: #38bdf8;">Methodology & Technical Approach</h2>
      <div id="methods-ig" class="ig-container"></div>
    </div>

    <div class="section full-width large-content">
      <h2 class="section-title" style="color: #facc15;">Key Findings</h2>
      <div id="findings-ig" class="ig-container large"></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <script src="/app/vendor/infographic.min.js"></script>
  <script>
    const igMethods = new AntVInfographic.Infographic({
      container: '#methods-ig',
      width: '100%',
      height: '100%',
    });
    const methodsSyntax = `infographic sequence-interaction-default-compact-card
data
  title Multi-Modal Connectomics Pipeline
  sequences
    - label 1. Imaging Modality
      children
        - label Serial-Section EM
          id img-em
          step 0
          desc 4 x 4 x 30 nm resolution
    - label 2. Computational Segregation
      children
        - label Deep Learning Tracing
          id ai-tracing
          step 1
          desc Automated neuron reconstruction
        - label Synapse Detection
          id ai-synapse
          step 1
          desc CNN Classifier (94.2% accuracy)
    - label 3. Circuit Analysis
      children
        - label Graph-Theoretic Clustering
          id analysis-motif
          step 2
          desc Motif detection algorithms
    - label 4. Functional Validation
      children
        - label Calcium & Optogenetics
          id val-calc
          step 3
          desc in vivo verification
  relations
    img-em - Raw Volumes -> ai-tracing
    img-em - Raw Volumes -> ai-synapse
    ai-tracing - Segments -> analysis-motif
    ai-synapse - Synapses -> analysis-motif
    analysis-motif - Predictions -> val-calc
theme
  palette #38bdf8 #8b5cf6 #ec4899 #facc15`;

    igMethods.render(methodsSyntax);

    const igFindings = new AntVInfographic.Infographic({
      container: '#findings-ig',
      width: '100%',
      height: '100%',
    });
    const findingsSyntax = `infographic list-grid-badge-card
data
  title Fundamental Principles of Neural Circuit Organization
  lists
    - label 37 Distinct Motifs
      desc Identified as recurring building blocks of larger circuits, suggesting a modular wiring logic analogous to digital logic gates.
      icon polygon
    - label Hub Neurons (3.5%)
      desc Comprising only ~3.5% of the population but accounting for over 28% of total synaptic output, indicating highly non-uniform influence.
      icon star
    - label Layer-Specific Rules
      desc Layer 5 enriched in recurrent connections (4.7:1 recurrent-to-feedforward ratio), while layers 2/3 -> 4 are feedforward dominated.
      icon layers
    - label Inhibitory Specificity
      desc Inhibitory interneurons formed connections with 6.2x higher specificity than excitatory neurons, challenging broad blanket assumptions.
      icon filter
theme
  palette #facc15 #38bdf8 #2dd4bf #ec4899`;

    igFindings.render(findingsSyntax);
  </script>
</body>
</html>
EOF

